On this extended EP—the first release for Skrillex's high-octane OWSLA label—North Carolina's Porter Robinson takes a no-holds-barred approach, experimenting freely with dubstep, trance, moombahton, and electro-house. It’s the sonic equivalent of walking between headlining sets at your favorite EDM festival. Tracks like "Vandalism" and "Unison" veer from beautiful, uplifting melodies to hard-as-nails drums and bass, while remixes from famous DJ friends like Knife Party and Kill the Noise promise to keep the party going hard and strong late into the night.
