A R I Z O N A's glossy synth-pop debut beats to the rhythm of an EDM heart. Though based in New Jersey, the trio add some of the heat and mystique of their namesake to an intoxicating brew of bubbly, '80s-inspired grooves built on big, bassy beats. Singer Zach Hannah's breathy, falsetto-laced croons sizzle with the intimate intensity of The Weeknd on sleek, hushed confessionals like "I Was Wrong" and "Electric Touch," then hint at classic Phil Collins on the slow-burning ballad "Are You."
